(accompanying certificate packet. Failed preliminary computations are) Tj T*
(not proof inputs. The final coverage file has status PASS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. OCCURRENCE AND THE DEGREE CONDITION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The rational torsion primes 2,3,5,7 occur after extension to any field) Tj T*
(of degree 13. For each p=11,13,17,19,23,29,31,37, occurrences.json) Tj T*
(records an irreducible polynomial f of degree 13 and rational functions) Tj T*
(x=a, y=g\(a\)/h\(a\), where f\(a\)=0. Put) Tj T*
( r=\(x^2*y-x*y+y-1\)/\(x^2*y-x\), s=\(x*y-y+1\)/\(x*y\),) Tj T*
( b=r*s*\(r-1\), c=s*\(r-1\).) Tj T*
(Then E: Y^2+\(1-c\)XY-bY=X^3-bX^2 has the point P=\(0,0\).) Tj T*
(verify_occurrences.m proves that f is irreducible over Q, E is) Tj T*
(nonsingular, P is nonzero, and p*P=0, for all eight examples. Thus) Tj T*
(these are exact degree-13 occurrence certificates, not deductions) Tj T*
(from occurrence in a different degree.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The example at 37 is a van Hoeij degree-13 place. Its x-coordinate) Tj T*
(satisfies) Tj T*
( x^13-4*x^12-x^11+10*x^10+3*x^9-21*x^8+3*x^7+24*x^6) Tj T*
( -15*x^5-10*x^4+12*x^3-x^2-3*x+1=0.) Tj T*
(Its y-coordinate, and the remaining examples, are recorded explicitly.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Conversely, a prime p dividing E\(K\)_tors is the order of a K-rational) Tj T*
(point. Its point on X_1\(p\) has degree dividing 13. For p>37 it cannot) Tj T*
(have degree 1, by the rational torsion theorem. Therefore it has degree) Tj T*
(13. Let D be its irreducible rational trace divisor on X_1\(p\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
