(The integral coefficient pairing identifies M with the Z_2-dual of) Tj T*
(\(T/I\) tensor Z_2. Raynaud's theorem gives) Tj T*
(                         2M subset L subset M.) Tj T*
(We do not assume L=M or an optimal-quotient formal immersion at 2.) Tj T*
(The precise lattice argument and references are reproduced in the) Tj T*
(packet's earlier dyadic theorem.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Put m=26 and) Tj T*
( T'_n=sum_{a|n} mu\(n/a\)T_a, L_n=T'_\(2n\)-2*T'_n.) Tj T*
(The integral spans of L_1,...,L_m and \(T_2-3\)T_1,...,\(T_2-3\)T_m) Tj T*
